<title>JAPAN: TENNIS-JAPAN OPEN FIRST ROUND RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-JAPAN OPEN FIRST ROUND RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>First round results in the  $1.22 million Japan Open tennis championships on Monday (Prefix denotes seedings):</p>
<p>Men</p>
<p>Martin Sinner (Germany) beat Andrei Olhovskiy (Russia) 6-3 6-4</p>
<p>Oliver Delaitre (France) beat Roger Smith (Bahamas) 6-7 (5-7) 6-3 6-3</p>
<p>Carsten Arriens (Germany) beat Yasufumi Yamamoto (Japan) 6-2 7-5</p>
<p>Jean Philippe Fleurian (France) beat Jim Grabb (U.S.) 6-3 6-2</p>
<p>Sebastien Lareau (Canada) beat Stephane Simian (France) 6-3 6-2</p>
<p>Takao Suzuki (Japan) beat Arne Thoms (Germany) 6-4 6-2</p>
<p>Jerome Golmard (France) beath Doug Flach (U.S.) 6-2 6-4</p>
<p>Henrik Holm (Sweden) beat Michael Joyce (U.S.) 4-6 6-3 7-5</p>
<p>Razvan Sabau (Romania) beat Thomas Shimada (Japan) 6-2 6-2</p>
<p>Frederik Fetterlein (Denmark) beat Goichi Motomura (Japan) 3-6 6-4 6-3</p>
<p>Women</p>
<p>Rika Hiraki (Japan) beat Rita Grande (Italy) 6-1 5-7 6-3</p>
<p>Miho Saeki (Japan) beat 8-Tamarine Tanasugarn (Thailand) 6-3 6-4</p>
<p>Yuka Yoshida (Japan) beat Andrea Glass (Germany) 6-1 4-1 (Glass retired injured)</p>
<p>Corina Morariu (U.S.) beat Sung Hee Park (South Korea) 6-3 6-2</p>
<p>Meilen Tu (U.S.) beat Alexi Dechaume-Balleret (France) 6-4 6-0</p>
<p>4-Ai Sugiyama (Japan) beat Ginger Helgeson-Nielsen (U.S.) 6-3 7-5</p>
<p>5-Wang Shi-ting (Taiwan) beat Haruka Inoue (Japan) 6-1 6-1</p>
</text>
